  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "ParseOldAtomList",
    "file": "rdkit/Code/GraphMol/FileParsers/MolFileParser.cpp",
    "description": "The legacy V2000 atom-list parser indexes fixed offsets in an unvalidated input string. In the invalid modifier branch for `switch (text[4])`, its diagnostic mistakenly reads `text[14]` (line 253) instead of the modifier at `text[4]`. A short malformed property line therefore causes an out-of-bounds read from the small-string stack storage while constructing the exception. The function also assumes `text[4]` and later fixed-width fields exist, so it should validate the legacy atom-list line length before any indexing/substrings; the immediate crashing access should report `text[4]`, not `text[14]`.",
    "conditions": "The fuzzer-controlled stream must parse as a V2000 molecule with at least one atom, then provide a nonempty first property line whose first character is not `M`, `A`, `V`, `G`, or `S`, causing `ParseMolBlockProperties()` to treat it as an old-style atom list. Its first three characters must parse to a 1-based atom index within the molecule, its character at offset 4 must be neither `T` nor `F`, and the line must be too short for offset 14 (as in this PoV). This selects the default modifier-error path and the erroneous `text[14]` diagnostic read triggers the stack-buffer-overflow."
  },
